CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=8a009144-7fb64372-017f-f2fa77e0-000007ea:Runton\, R
 ajashi
CREATED:20260503T062521Z
DESCRIPTION:We have witnessed an explosion in the capabilities of foundati
 on models and artificial intelligence to reason and generate content in t
 he digital domain. Despite these advancements\, there still exists a fund
 amental disconnect between their intelligence and our everyday physical e
 nvironments. To bridge this gap and create truly ubiquitous intelligent e
 nvironments that are capable of supporting everything from smart living f
 or aging populations to autonomous urban management\, we need to design a
 nd deploy adaptable\, context-aware AI on the edge that can perceive\, ac
 t\, and operate robustly in complex physical environments. Towards this v
 ision\, I will present several lines of work that 1) exploit the physical
  interaction between robotic agents and their environment to perform auto
 nomous\, sensorless mapping of 3D airflow fields using only the flight dy
 namics of low-cost micro-drones\, 2) democratize the deployment of adapta
 ble edge sensing through a modular\, plug-and-play IoT sensing system tha
 t enables the rapid\, accessible integration of customized hardware for A
 I-driven applications\, and 3) demonstrate how interfacing modern foundat
 ion models with a reconfigurable drone enables embodied agents to autonom
 ously perceive\, understand\, and adapt to diverse physical tasks.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260503T062521Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260506T120000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260503T062521Z
